WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.130
So this is your true self?

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.510
A fluidic organism from the planet Jacqueline Ess.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.020
Its name is Clive.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.430
It has an incredibly vast ability to mimic things.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.810
Do you find it hideous as well?

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.700
Yeah... I can't call it pretty...

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.830
Indeed...

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.730
But, thank you. It was brave of you to show me your true self.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.080
You're... a good person.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.060
It is I who should give you thanks.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:52.830
Thank you.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.230
Hey, where are you going?

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:04.600
I'm leaving. I can't bother you any further.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.110
Wait... If you leave now, you'll be cau-

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.450
Oh, but you can transform!

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.860
Wait a moment. I can transform?

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:20.160
You just said so... Your name is Clive and you have the ability to mimic things...

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.440
You're saying that <i>I'm</i> Clive?!

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:23.270
Yeah, <i>you</i>!

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.910
That's my pet.

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:26.080
What?

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.400
You just said that was your true self!

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.600
I meant owning that sort of pet defines who I truly am.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.080
Somebody's jumpin' to conclusions!

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.460
Then, your memories?

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.830
Haven't returned one bit.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.990
Well then, better decide who gets which room!

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.730
So you're stayin' after all?!

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:48.200
Presently, there are hundreds of alien species coming and going, living their lives on Earth.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.350
Species that come in peace...

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.070
Aggressive, warlike species...

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:57.260
All kinds of alien species coexist with us, maintaining a precarious balance.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:01.570
And the only ones who don't realize this... are us humans!

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:03.720
Yukitaka?

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:05.370
Yukitaka!

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:06.470
What is it?

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.200
You got a girl you like?

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.120
Go to sleep!

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:18.770
The towns entrance is adorned with a cows skull

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:23.730
It's fine that the law is decided by the strongest,

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:28.720
But this simple feeling will not be enough to fulfill you

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.200
Everyone will definitely revolt and shortly disappear

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:39.480
That's a shocking bloody picture

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.630
I'm feeling nauseous

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:54.840
Holding my head, I board the subway

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:05.280
Righteous way of living, righteous way of dying

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:15.730
Who on earth knows or what the hell can show me?

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:25.920
Cold finger girl

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.070
Sit Down

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.770
Warning, warning.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:13.250
Yamagata prefecture in the country of Japan is controlled by Disckonians.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.270
Withdraw immediately.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.100
Repeat:

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.940
Yamagata prefecture in the country of Japan...

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:19.830
Captain...

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.330
What?

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.900
It just said Disckonians, didn't it?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.360
This is bad! We have to get permission quickly, or...

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.990
Those guys are really protective of their territory.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:32.840
I know!

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.530
Why did he have to crash land here of all places?

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:37.850
That damn Baka!

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.880
Captain!

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.650
You are aware that such an outburst warrants a court martial.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.780
Am not!

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.950
When we find him, restrain me first!

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.070
I'm not confident I'll be able to restrain myself!

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.360
Shut up!

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:55.190
Sade, contact the leader of the Disckonians immediately.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:55.860
Right.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.650
Colin, you go capture that man right away.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.380
That man?

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.390
You know who I'm talking about!

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.570
R-Right!

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:27.720
You're freakin' me out.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.540
Miho-chan, what's the matter?

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:37.340
Sorry, I just heard some weird laughter...

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:40.060
Oh, I'm sorry... I was on the phone and...

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.480
The picture of the person the police were looking for

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.210
looked a lot like the man with you last night, Tsutsui-kun.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:50.190
T-That's just a...

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.870
Eyesight: 20-20.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.180
Could he be an alien?

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:00.230
Nicknamed the "Missing Hunters",

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.970
they're a special investigative team that works for my father's laboratory.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:09.760
I wonder if he's reading data from NASA or something.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:10.860
You're kidding me...

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.090
Anyway, he shouldn't go outside.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.420
You're going to help me?

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.120
Yeah.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:19.360
It's not that I'm rebelling against my father or anything...

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.870
I just don't like the forceful way they do everything.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.290
You got that right.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.090
Huh?

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:32.580
Doesn't seem like they've bugged the place.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.800
I can only imagine how she was raised...

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:38.970
It's boring being stuck in here on such a lovely day...

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.110
Let's hang out somewhere.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.930
You don't get it, do you?!

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:45.870
You're being pursued by those laboratory guys!

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.180
I hate being bored.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.420
Deal with it!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:52.500
Then take this and perform for my amusement.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.980
You some kind of king?

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.780
Yes, something like that... though not exactly...

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:58.660
Don't worry about it.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.370
Just stay put and be quiet.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.940
Until help comes, it's best to stay here.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.670
Help? Someone's coming?

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:10.220
I don't remember how I came to this planet.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:14.690
For all I know, I may be the last remaining member of my species.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:24.000
Is he going to be okay? Maybe you went too far?

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.680
Nah. When I worry, he just makes a fool out of me.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.850
It sure is quiet.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:34.570
Yeah.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.130
Don't tell me he-

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.740
He did!

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:47.720
"Dear Yukitaka,"

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:50.120
"How are you? Enjoying yourself?"

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.590
"Having a blast?"

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.720
"Anything going on right now?"...

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:55.170
What the...

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.830
He's just screwing with us!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.300
While we were worrying about him he was plotting something!

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.140
We're not gonna look for him?

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.680
It's not our problem! He's on his own!

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:05.720
But...

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:08.710
Tsutsui-kun...

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:09.230
What?

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:12.930
The laboratory is connected with the government.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:17.480
If they're ordered to, they'll kill him when they find him.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.970
Will you really be okay with that?

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:39.590
We would like to speak with your chief, Sakamoto Jinpachi-san.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.370
So you're here?

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:46.600
Well then, sit down and have a rest.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:52.090
I see.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.730
There was an accident on the mothership, eh?

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:58.070
Thankfully, we avoided any significant disaster,

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:02.180
but a young man jumped the gun and took off in an escape pod on his own.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.790
It seems like he had an emergency landing near this area.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:12.050
Couldn't you have been a bit more skilled about it?

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:19.340
The people from your planet have ships that can avoid radar, and shield themselves from detection...

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:21.000
We're really sorry.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.020
We'll take all possible precautions.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.480
Whatever is appropriate...

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.990
Hey! We have guests.

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:28.610
Pipe down over there!

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:32.770
These men are Craft-san and Sade-san from the planet Dogura!

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:34.930
Howdy!

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.830
Gramps, are we fightin' the Dogurians this time?

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.360
Captain...

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:45.770
Now, now... These people just came here looking for someone.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:49.270
No more butting in, got it?

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.620
Aww... How boring.

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:55.760
Dogurians are all peaceful, so they can't fight.

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.820
Lame!

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.980
Eh, please don't mind them.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:03.380
We understand.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:08.870
Though, all the blokes from my planet are hotheads...

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:13.070
If something were to happen, there'd be no stopping them, I suspect.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:16.960
In which case...

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:21.090
...they crush whoever they're up against.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:22.720
I see...

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:28.050
Thank you for coming all this way.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:29.320
No, thank you, sir.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:35.180
But to go so far as to learn the local language of a backwoods planet...

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:39.570
That person in the escape pod must be someone important, eh?

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:40.680
Y-Yes...

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.460
No! He is nothing but a commoner!

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:44.770
Is he now?

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:46.880
What's so funny?

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:48.720
Please excuse us!

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.090
Captain, picking fights is not going to help the situation.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:11:00.000
They're an extremely aggressive species that has wiped out hundreds of others!

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.370
I know!

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:21.680
God <i>damn</i> they piss me off!

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.470
It is strange, however.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.910
I have never seen Disckonians so well-behaved.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:31.050
And I have heard that there are Ellerians on this planet, too.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:32.910
Ellerians?

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.720
Oh, you mean their arch enemy?

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:37.250
Yes.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:42.490
Earth is the only planet where Ellerians and Disckonians can live together.

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:43.850
Is there something special here?

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:47.880
It's a mystery, even to interplanetary ecology scholars.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:54.480
The only certainty is that they have made it a rule not to lay hands on Earthlings.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:55.740
Why is that?

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.370
Colin? Have you caught him yet?

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:06.340
I've located the origin of the distress call,

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:08.210
but he's not there.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.520
Also, it's just a normal apartment.

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:14.640
It looks like he's living together with some Earthling...

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.160
It looks like he's living together with some Earthling...

00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:18.930
That Baka!

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.270
Use mine.

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:22.650
Colin, standby on alert!

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.190
We are going after him!

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.790
Wouldn't it be better for us to stake out the apartment as well?

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:35.150
I'm not a biologist like you.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:38.160
When it comes to <i>him</i>, I know what I'm doing!

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:38.960
Right...

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:42.640
When it comes to him, we must assume the worst-case scenario.

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:45.790
He's always gonna go a bit above the diagonal!

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:47.260
Right...

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.920
Do you have this in extra large?

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:51.840
Yes!

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.270
Just give it a rest!

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.440
Man, that was exciting!

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.190
There sure was a lot of security.

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:30.800
Security? Where?

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.630
You didn't notice?

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.410
There were cameras set up,

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:41.390
and the couple taking pictures and the tractor driver were most likely guards.

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:42.640
Seriously?

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:44.980
He really is an alien!

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.310
I bet Father must be really excited.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:53.400
But if he didn't go back there, where'd he go?

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.060
Anyway, let's have a strategy meeting in that café.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.370
Okay, sure!

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:04.050
Sir?

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.670
Hey!

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:16.840
"Hey" my ass!

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.100
Do you know how much we looked for you, jerk?

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.890
Just sitting there... It was so unnerving...

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:30.030
So you went and bought new clothes and had some spaghetti Napolitan at a café?!

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.360
It's not Napolitan, it's Penne Arrabiata.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.010
I don't give a rat's ass!

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:38.360
That kick... Is Yukitaka-kun perhaps...

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:45.720
Actually, I'm dealing with something very difficult right now.

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.750
Yeah yeah, me too.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.630
So maybe we could talk about it?

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.380
As if, idiot.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:51.870
Yukitaka-kun!

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:59.460
I want you two to decide if what I'm about to tell you was a good thing, or a bad thing.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:04.200
A certain man was walking down the street after doing some shopping.

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.790
You mean you, right?

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:10.200
This man was being chased by a certain organization.

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:13.000
It's obviously you you're talking about!

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:17.120
He wanted nothing more than to avoid causing any trouble.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.370
You're talkin' about <i>you</i>, damn it! Admit it!

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:21.030
What does it matter? Let it go!

00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:22.540
And then...

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:27.280
Come on, it'll just take 10 minutes.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:27.900
I said no!

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.120
It'll be lotsa fun, we promise!

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.500
No! Let go of me!

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.300
Well then, it's settled! Off we go!

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:35.670
And? And?

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:40.350
The person wanted to avoid trouble, so continued on by.

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:43.300
Yeah, guess that's all you norms can do.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:44.350
I knew it.

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:49.170
But after he saw this, he began to reconsider. He had to stop them.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:53.440
Forcing someone to come with you against their will is wrong.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:58.160
What do you think, former punk Tsutsui-san?

00:15:58.160 --> 00:15:59.950
It's disgusting.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:05.580
But if you look at it from the other side it's only natural to call him an idiot.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:05.450
Yup, he's a former punk.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.660
In response, he said...

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.410
Beat it!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.140
And, there you have it.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:16.780
If he was serious business he'd beat the crap out of him without saying a word.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:19.820
If he did that the woman would be scared shitless, too.

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:25.300
But that person instead strongly responded "Let her go!"

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.680
Wait, seriously?

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.080
And when he did...

00:16:33.060 --> 00:16:35.770
While enduring the intense pain,

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:40.690
he saw that the woman had escaped to safety, and concluded he'd done a good thing.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:45.510
Afterwards, he only had to wait for them to tire of hitting him.

00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:46.660
However...

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:50.220
As they were quite persistent...

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:02.750
He punched one out!

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:04.970
With all his might...

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:08.510
He couldn't help it! It was for that girl's sake, after all.

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:12.570
But to answer violence with violence...

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:16.170
And the others saw the blue blood and ran off...

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:21.030
Don't worry about that. Punks like those will forget it all in a jiffy.

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:22.360
You think so?

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:24.460
Don't look so down!

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:26.790
I really think I misjudged you!

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.860
Then, what's your verdict?

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:35.120
It was a good thing!

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:38.830
Thank goodness!

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.380
Then, after that...

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:43.880
I just need to figure out what to do with this.

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:47.880
Thankfully, the two that escaped didn't notice it.

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:51.970
Even if they can't get in touch with him, they probably won't go to the police first.

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:57.390
Therefore, it may be best to carry it deep into the mountains and bury it.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.520
Yukitaka, what do you think?

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:01.900
Call. The. Police!

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:04.890
But why?

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.240
I thought I did a good thing!

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.970
Shut the hell up!

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:09.990
Nobody said anything about <i>this</i>!

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:11.870
But if I did, I would have frightened you...

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:12.950
Duh!

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:17.370
What'll we do?

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:20.170
I am quite sure they can't trace us.

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:22.240
I didn't leave any physical evidence.

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.180
Playing the good guy to the end, are we?

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:27.030
Captain, they've returned.

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:29.540
It's him all right.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.020
W-Who are you?

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:34.790
There you are!

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.110
Prince?!

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.900
Prince?

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:42.560
Yukitaka, who are they?

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:46.260
He lost his memories?

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:49.070
And is wanted for murder?

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:50.740
Yes...

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:53.510
But wait, he's a <i>prince</i>?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:55.830
Surprised, peons?

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.510
See, Sade...

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:03.540
It's just like I said, right?

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:06.360
This guy always goes above the diagonal!

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:08.590
What'll we do?

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:12.010
Does it matter? Restrain him and force him onto the space ship.

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:14.390
Wait, I don't understand at all.

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:16.900
What are you people?

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:18.410
Where did you come from?

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.110
You'll know once your memories come back.

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:25.100
Now then, come with me.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:26.280
No, I refuse.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:28.350
Stop complainin' and get over 'ere!

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.560
Hold it!

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.930
He said he lost his memories!

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:34.740
Explain to him!

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.870
He's the prince of your planet, right?

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:40.780
That is of no concern for a citizen of some undeveloped planet!

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:41.980
Shut it.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:46.920
He crashed landed on Earth, was chased while still knowing nothing,

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.150
and came here after being injured!

00:19:49.150 --> 00:19:53.140
He's uneasy without his memories! Can't you understand?

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:54.660
Understand?

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:58.140
It's you who doesn't understand!

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:02.390
He's a devil! And has an extremely difficult personality.

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:03.660
Say that again, punk?

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:06.490
If I could, I'd love to just abandon him here.

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:09.160
However, I have to take him with me,

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:12.210
in order to save the universe from destruction...

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:17.110
We were in the middle of escorting the prince to a conference.

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:21.160
It is the largest such conference in the universe,

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:26.850
and even the militant factions have decided to attend.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.670
If the prince of Dogura is late,

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.100
and the conference is affected...

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:39.340
It will not be only our planet, but thousands of planets that face destruction.

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.890
Understand, brat?

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:45.440
Then say that in the first place, you haughty bastard...

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:47.060
Now, now...

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:49.090
I have no duty to explain to people from an undeveloped planet!

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:53.950
It was you people who crashed landed here and caused all this trouble, Slick!

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:55.630
Oh, yeah?

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:57.230
You wanna die, punk?

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:59.480
Sure, let's do this. Right here.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:00.830
Don't you dare spit on me, trash.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:03.650
Screw you! You know he actually <i>killed</i> someone.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.060
Show me proof, monkey.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:09.020
Proof, proof? Is your planet full of preschoolers?

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:11.440
You're just copying what that Baka said, aren't you?

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:13.330
There's a body, smart-ass!

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.880
Then bring it here, bozo! You do and I'll prostrate myself and beg your forgiveness!

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.290
<i>You</i> bring it here, bitch!

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:18.510
Shut up and die!

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.720
I'm baack!

00:21:18.510 --> 00:21:19.720
You die!

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:20.380
Oh, yeah?

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.970
Yo mama's so fat!

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:23.230
But you've never seen her!

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:28.260
Phew, that was heavy.

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:32.040
What the hell have brought in here?!

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.570
But someone might find it.

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:34.650
And?!

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:36.560
I'm so sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:37.950
Is this good enough for ya?

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:38.940
Are you listening?

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:41.180
Say something, damn you!

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:44.140
You can't say nothin' now, eh?

00:21:44.140 --> 00:21:47.000
Captain, we have a problem.

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:48.750
What is it?

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:50.760
It is extremely bad.

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:53.010
This is not a human.

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:56.760
It is a Disckonian.

00:21:57.380 --> 00:22:00.500
All the blokes from my planet are hotheads...

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:04.140
If something were to happen, there'd be no stopping them, I suspect.

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:08.270
In which case, they crush whomever they're up against.

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:27.740
Are you ready?

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:38.250
Do not fear 'The Now' searching for something that can't be seen across this infinite distance

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:52.470
Under the hundred million glittering lights, I found you searching for your dream

00:22:52.470 --> 00:23:01.230
An infinite world filled with glass shards

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:13.290
Growing up I felt I knew many meaningless things

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:20.750
Shining like a jewel, you soar in the sky, no past, no future

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:26.090
The answer is beyond the sky

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:36.600
Do not fear 'The Dream', in a distant
place where truth and lies are unseen

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:52.330
Under the hundred million glittering lights, flowers sway in the wind

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:59.720
There's no more running or hiding.

00:23:59.720 --> 00:24:00.470
You going to kill him?

00:24:00.470 --> 00:24:03.350
We will take the culprit into our custody.

00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:05.840
He's just a commoner, yes?

00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:06.990
They're gonna kill us!

00:24:06.990 --> 00:24:09.720
We swear on the pride of our race!

00:24:09.720 --> 00:24:11.340
We will kill you!

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:12.460
I get it, I'll go.

00:24:12.630 --> 00:24:15.330
Everything will be settled if I sacrifice myself, yes?

00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:16.070
You're awful.

00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:18.940
Next time: Risky Game!

00:24:18.940 --> 00:24:20.570
So he was only pretending to be dead?
